# Budget ceilings (apps/budget tool): the OS must stay out of the way.
# The system = used memory (like free) minus the user's work.
#   system  <MB>          ceiling of the whole system (kernel, daemons, niri session, bar...)
#   process <MB>          default ceiling of one system program (all its processes together)
#   limit   <name> <MB>   ceiling of one program (name as shown by `budget`, 15 characters max)
#   apps    <prefixes>    the user's work, outside the budget, with everything it starts (containers too)
#   terminals <names>     whatever is started from the shell of one of these terminals counts as work
# A layer (users/<login>/dotfiles/config/budget/limits) replaces this file.
system 1024
process 150
limit niri 250
apps chrome chromium firefox claude node podman conmon qemu
terminals foot
